Additional User-Agent condition

The permission granted above is also subject to this condition:

A "Modified Build" is an executable built from source code that has been
modified from a version of the Software published by the copyright holders,
other than a build published by the copyright holders as an official gn-cli
build. Compiling unchanged source with a different compiler, platform or
build configuration does not, by itself, make a build a Modified Build.

When making, using or distributing a Modified Build, you must ensure that
every HTTP request it sends uses either:

(a) a custom User-Agent that identifies the modified client distinctly from
    official gn-cli builds; or
(b) a User-Agent containing the literal substring "_fork".

This requirement also applies when reusing saved sessions or credentials.
The additional condition must be preserved with the permission notice in
all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

This licence covers the CLI software, not access to the hosted NextGen
services. Use of those services remains subject to their applicable terms.
Third-party components remain under their respective licences, as listed
in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.
